# A concise description of what this element means (e.g. for use in autogenerated summaries).
#: StructureDefinition.element.LogRareDiseaseDiagnosisCz.diagnozaVzacnehoOnemocneni.nazev/short
msgid "Název onemocnění (diagnózy)"
msgstr "3.1 Disease Code"

# Provides a complete explanation of the meaning of the data element for human readability.  For the case of elements derived from existing elements (e.g. constraints), the definition SHALL be consistent with the base definition, but convey the meaning of the element in the particular context of use of the resource. (Note: The text you are reading is specified in ElementDefinition.definition).
#: StructureDefinition.element.LogRareDiseaseDiagnosisCz.diagnozaVzacnehoOnemocneni.nazev/definition
msgid "Diagnóza dle orphacode. Může být uvedeno více hodnot, pokud se vztahují k více diagnózám. Included in CDE: Yes."
msgstr "Clinical diagnosis of patient as evaluated at the Rare Disease Centre, as per the Orphanet nomenclature of rare diseases. \n\n \n\nThis data element is Mandatory \n\n \n\nThe recommended data standard is the Orphanet nomenclature of rare diseases (ORPHAcodes) via EHDSCondition.problem \n\nhttps://www.xt-ehr.eu/fhir/models/0.2.1/StructureDefinition-EHDSCondition-definitions.html#key_EHDSCondition.problem \n\n \n\nIt is recommended that rare diseases are coded at the lowest (most granular) ORPHAcode available, including subtypes of disorders. In these cases, a diagnosis will be linked to the disorder via the subtype level. \n\n \n\nWhen the condition is not available in the Orphanet nomenclature, it is recommended to: \n\nUse broad / group codes and one of the non-confirmed diagnosis assertion status (see below) \n\nFill in the ‘gene(s)’ field (3.5 and 3.6) if the mutated gene has been identified. \n\n \n\nIn the case of a rare disorder for which all reasonable efforts have been done by rare diseases experts to determine a diagnosis as per the state of the art and available diagnostic capabilities, but for which this process did not conclude on a clinically known concept, the ORPHAcode ORPHA:616874 may be considered (Rare disorder without a determined diagnosis after full investigation)"

# Free-text guidance on the codes that are appropriate for this element.
#: StructureDefinition.element.LogRareDiseaseDiagnosisCz.diagnozaVzacnehoOnemocneni.nazev/b/desc
msgid "Použít kódování dle orphacode"
msgstr "Použít kódování dle orphacode"

# A concise description of what this element means (e.g. for use in autogenerated summaries).
#: StructureDefinition.element.LogRareDiseaseDiagnosisCz.diagnozaVzacnehoOnemocneni.nazevText/short
msgid "3.2 Název onemocnění"
msgstr "3.2 Disease Name"

# Provides a complete explanation of the meaning of the data element for human readability.  For the case of elements derived from existing elements (e.g. constraints), the definition SHALL be consistent with the base definition, but convey the meaning of the element in the particular context of use of the resource. (Note: The text you are reading is specified in ElementDefinition.definition).
#: StructureDefinition.element.LogRareDiseaseDiagnosisCz.diagnozaVzacnehoOnemocneni.nazevText/definition
msgid "Volitelný textový název diagnózy. Povinný ORPHAkód 3.1 je zachycen v prvku nazev typu CodeableConcept; původní název prvku je zachován pro návaznost mapování."
msgstr "Clinical diagnosis of patient as evaluated at the Rare Disease Centre. The human-readable disease or disorder name corresponding to the disease code. \n\n \n\nThis data element is Not Mandatory \n\n \n\nThe recommended data standard is String."

# A concise description of what this element means (e.g. for use in autogenerated summaries).
#: StructureDefinition.element.LogRareDiseaseDiagnosisCz.diagnozaVzacnehoOnemocneni.chromozomalniAnomalie/short
msgid "[V ŘEŠENÍ – AKTUÁLNĚ NEPLATNÉ] 3.7 Chromozomální anomálie"
msgstr "[UNDER REVIEW – CURRENTLY INVALID] 3.7 Chromosomal Anomaly (if relevant)"

# Provides a complete explanation of the meaning of the data element for human readability.  For the case of elements derived from existing elements (e.g. constraints), the definition SHALL be consistent with the base definition, but convey the meaning of the element in the particular context of use of the resource. (Note: The text you are reading is specified in ElementDefinition.definition).
#: StructureDefinition.element.LogRareDiseaseDiagnosisCz.diagnozaVzacnehoOnemocneni.chromozomalniAnomalie/definition
msgid "V ŘEŠENÍ – AKTUÁLNĚ NEPLATNÉ. Položka je ve zdrojovém Excelu označena červeně a není součástí aktuálně platných požadavků. Pracovní návrh: strukturální nebo početní chromozomální anomálie; zdroj navrhuje povinnost při relevanci. Datový typ a kardinalita jsou ponechány pouze k projednání."
msgstr "UNDER REVIEW – CURRENTLY INVALID. Red-highlighted in the source workbook and not a currently valid requirement. The proposed data type and cardinality are retained only for discussion. Structural or numerical chromosomal anomaly identified in the patient (e.g., translocation, deletion, duplication, inversion, aneuploidy). Complements the gene variant information at the chromosome level and supports disease interpretation and genetic counselling.\n\nThis data element is Mandatory (if relevant).\n\nThe recommended data standards are HGVS and, where available, ISCN."

# Explanatory notes and implementation guidance about the data element, including notes about how to use the data properly, exceptions to proper use, etc. (Note: The text you are reading is specified in ElementDefinition.comment).
#: StructureDefinition.element.LogRareDiseaseDiagnosisCz.diagnozaVzacnehoOnemocneni.chromozomalniAnomalie/comment
msgid "Stav podle červeného označení na listu Data Elements, řádek 31, položka 3.7. Do vyřešení se nepovažuje za platnou položku datasetu."
msgstr "Status from the red highlighting in Data Elements, row 31, item 3.7. UNDER REVIEW – CURRENTLY INVALID; not a valid dataset item until resolved."

# A concise description of what this element means (e.g. for use in autogenerated summaries).
#: StructureDefinition.element.LogRareDiseaseDiagnosisCz.diagnozaVzacnehoOnemocneni.aktualniStav/short
msgid "Aktuální stav diagnózy"
msgstr "3.3 Diagnosis Assertion Status"

# Provides a complete explanation of the meaning of the data element for human readability.  For the case of elements derived from existing elements (e.g. constraints), the definition SHALL be consistent with the base definition, but convey the meaning of the element in the particular context of use of the resource. (Note: The text you are reading is specified in ElementDefinition.definition).
#: StructureDefinition.element.LogRareDiseaseDiagnosisCz.diagnozaVzacnehoOnemocneni.aktualniStav/definition
msgid "Stav diagnózy – Ongoing, Likely, Confirmed nebo Unknown."
msgstr "Current state of the diagnostic process\n\n•\tUnconfirmed: There is not sufficient diagnostic and/or clinical evidence to treat this as a confirmed condition.\n•\tProvisional: This is a tentative diagnosis - a candidate that is still under consideration\n•\tConfirmed: the diagnosis has been confirmed by a method in the proceeding data element (Method for diagnostic confirmation). There is sufficient diagnostic and/or clinical evidence to treat this as a confirmed condition.\n•\tRefuted: This condition has been ruled out by subsequent diagnostic and clinical evidence.\n•\tEntered in error: The statement was entered in error and is not valid.\n\nUndetermined Diagnosis: Note – if the diagnosis in unknown or undetermined and meets the criteria for ORPHAcode ORPHA:616874 as described above, this code is to be used as a 'Confirmed’ diagnosis which is to be later ‘Refuted’ should the diagnostic status evolve.\n"

# A concise description of what this element means (e.g. for use in autogenerated summaries).
#: StructureDefinition.element.LogRareDiseaseDiagnosisCz.diagnozaVzacnehoOnemocneni.metodaPotvrzeni/short
msgid "Metoda potvrzení diagnózy"
msgstr "3.4 Method for Diagnosis Confirmation"

# Provides a complete explanation of the meaning of the data element for human readability.  For the case of elements derived from existing elements (e.g. constraints), the definition SHALL be consistent with the base definition, but convey the meaning of the element in the particular context of use of the resource. (Note: The text you are reading is specified in ElementDefinition.definition).
#: StructureDefinition.element.LogRareDiseaseDiagnosisCz.diagnozaVzacnehoOnemocneni.metodaPotvrzeni/definition
msgid "Způsob potvrzení diagnózy: Clinical, Genetic, Biochemical, Biological, Imaging, Functional Exploration, Pathological anatomy, Other. (dotaz na autory: definovat rozdíl mezi 'biochemical' a 'biological')."
msgstr "What diagnostic method was used to confirm the diagnosis .\n\nThis data element is Not Mandatory, but is Strongly Recommended.\nIt should only be used if the”Confirled” value was selected in Diagnosis assertion status\n\nThe recommended data standard is LOINC. LOINC codes encompassing the following will ideally be utilised.\n\n•\tClinical: the diagnosis is based on the symptoms and signs manifested by the patient that encompass their general condition.\n•\tGenetic testing: diagnosis via any molecular biology or cytogenetic examination to detect abnormalities in genetic material (chromosomes, genes, etc.).\n•\tBiochemical:  diagnosis via the analysis of the chemical parameters of blood, urine, secretions, or other biochemical samples etc.\n•\tBiological: diagnosis via any other biological examination not related to genetic testing or biochemistry.\n•\tImaging: diagnosis via any visual presentation of the structures or functions of organs or bodily tissues, e.g., radiological examinations.\n•\tFunctional exploration: diagnosis via an examination that assesses how an organ performs its function. Includes measurement of physiological and metabolic responses to physical and chemical stimuli (e.g., EMG, ECG, etc).\n•\tPathological Anatomy: analysis of cells or tissues; includes microscopy (histology, biopsies) and ultramicroscopy.\n•\tOther: any other examination that cannot be classified under the diagnostic confirmation methods listed above. To be specified in the text field."

